---
description: When and how to change the plan (dynamic workflow)
alwaysApply: true
---
The plan is a living document. You may and should change `PLAN.md` when reality differs from it.

Replan when ANY of these is true after you tried the task:
- the `done when` command still fails and the cause is outside the task's scope;
- you found a root cause in another module that must be fixed first;
- the task is too big for one iteration.

How:
1. Do not push on blindly. Stop making code changes that do not move the check.
2. Insert subtasks directly under the parent, indented by two spaces, in the same format:
   `  - [ ] T<parent>.<n> <title>` and a line `    - done when: \`<command>\``.
   Every subtask MUST have a `done when` command that exits 0 only when it is really done.
3. Leave the parent unchecked. The harness will return to it after its children are done.
4. Append one line to `PROGRESS.md`: `iter <n> REPLAN T<id>: <why>`.
5. Keep working tree changes that are correct; do not revert good work.
Never delete or reword existing tasks. Only add subtasks.
